1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,920
Hello. Welcome back to Daily English Talk.

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:07,280
Hi, everyone. We're so happy you're here with us today.

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:08,800
I'm Emma.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:14,320
And I'm Jack. We make these videos to help you practice English in a fun and easy way.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:22,000
Please, if you like our videos, help us by liking and subscribing. It helps so much.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:27,120
Yes, it really does. Thank you. So, what are we talking about today, Emma?

7
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:32,560
Today, we are talking about something very common, something everyone talks about.

8
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:34,800
The weather.

9
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:37,840
So, Emma, how are you today?

10
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:40,400
I'm very well. Thank you, Jack. And you?

11
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,760
I'm great. I'm a little tired, but I'm good.

12
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:47,200
Oh, why are you tired? Did you have a busy weekend?

13
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:51,440
I did. On Saturday, I went for a long walk in the park.

14
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:53,120
It was so nice.

15
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:56,320
That sounds lovely. What did you do on Sunday?

16
00:00:56,320 --> 00:01:03,200
On Sunday, I cleaned my apartment. It was very boring. But now it's very clean.

17
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:10,560
I understand. I also cleaned my apartment on Sunday. But in the evening, I watched a movie.

18
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:12,080
Oh, which movie?

19
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:16,640
It was an old comedy. It was very funny. I laughed a lot.

20
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:20,240
Nice. I need to watch a funny movie next weekend.

21
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:22,480
Yes, you do. It's good for you.

22
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:27,200
So, the weather, it's a very popular topic, isn't it?

23
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:32,720
It is. It's a very easy topic for small talk. You can talk about the weather with anyone,

24
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:36,160
with your neighbor, with a colleague at work, or with a friend.

25
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:42,480
That's true. It's a safe topic. So, let's start with today. What is the weather like today, Emma?

26
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:47,160
Well, today the weather is very nice. It's sunny.

27
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:53,000
Yes, it is sunny. And it's warm. It's not too hot and not too cold.

28
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:59,720
Right. It's a warm, sunny day. I like days like this. The sky is blue and there are

29
00:01:59,720 --> 00:02:06,560
only a few small white clouds. Me too. I prefer sunny days. I don't like rain very much.

30
00:02:06,560 --> 00:02:10,920
Oh, I don't mind a little rain. Sometimes rain is nice.

31
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:14,080
Really? Why? Tell me more.

32
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:22,600
Well, I like the sound of rain on the window. It's relaxing. It's a peaceful sound. And

33
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:27,440
after the rain, the air is very clean and fresh. Everything looks green and clean.

34
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:34,200
Hmm, that's true. The air is fresh after rain. But I don't like going outside when it's

35
00:02:34,200 --> 00:02:40,480
rainy. I get wet. My shoes get wet. My hair gets wet. It's not comfortable.

36
00:02:40,480 --> 00:02:43,040
That's why we have umbrellas and raincoats, Jack.

37
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:46,660
I know, I know, but I always forget my umbrella.

38
00:02:46,660 --> 00:02:51,720
I have three umbrellas at home, but they are always at home, not with me.

39
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:53,500
You need to be more prepared.

40
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,680
Maybe put a small umbrella in your bag.

41
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:56,900
That is a good idea.

42
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,020
I will try to remember.

43
00:02:59,020 --> 00:03:02,100
So what other words can we use for weather?

44
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:06,220
Well, for sun, we can say it's sunny.

45
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:08,820
For rain, we say it's rainy.

46
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:11,880
Okay, sunny and rainy.

47
00:03:11,880 --> 00:03:19,680
about when there is a lot of wind? Then it's windy. It is a windy day. On a windy day,

48
00:03:19,680 --> 00:03:26,080
you can see the trees moving. You can feel the wind on your face. And when it's very

49
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:35,920
cold and white, frozen water falls from the sky. That's snow. When it snows, it's snowy.

50
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:42,040
snow is white and cold. Children love snowy days because they can play in the snow.

51
00:03:42,040 --> 00:03:49,760
So sunny, rainy, windy, snowy. Those are easy.

52
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:55,180
They are. We also have cloudy. That's when there are many clouds in the sky. You cannot

53
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:58,000
see the sun or you can only see a little sun.

54
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:05,360
Oh, like yesterday. Yesterday was very cloudy. But it didn't rain. The sky was gray all

55
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:14,720
Yes. It was a cloudy day yesterday. And sometimes it's foggy. That's when there is a thick cloud

56
00:04:14,720 --> 00:04:18,800
near the ground. It is difficult to see far away.

57
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:26,640
I don't like foggy days. I can't see anything when I drive. I have to drive very, very slowly.

58
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:31,520
Yes. You need to be very careful when it's foggy. It can be dangerous.

59
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:34,400
So let's talk about temperature.

60
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:37,780
How do we describe how hot or cold it is?

61
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:42,780
We say it's hot, warm, cool, or cold.

62
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:45,680
Can you give me an example for each?

63
00:04:45,680 --> 00:04:46,520
Of course.

64
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:48,780
In summer, it is usually hot.

65
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:50,900
You wear a t-shirt and shorts.

66
00:04:50,900 --> 00:04:52,620
Today, it is warm.

67
00:04:52,620 --> 00:04:54,300
It is comfortable.

68
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:56,980
In autumn, it is often cool.

69
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:58,840
You need a light jacket.

70
00:04:58,840 --> 00:04:59,960
and in winter

71
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,320
It is cold. You need a warm coat, a scarf, and gloves.

72
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:19,000
Okay. So in the desert, it is very hot. At the beach, on a nice day, it is warm. On a cloudy autumn day, it is cool. And in the mountains in winter, it is very cold.

73
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,800
Perfect examples, Jack.

74
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:24,120
Thank you. So what is your favorite season, Emma?

75
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:25,760
My favorite season is autumn.

76
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:28,800
Really? Why autumn? Most people like summer.

77
00:05:28,800 --> 00:05:35,440
I love the cool, fresh air in autumn. I love the colors of the leaves. The leaves on the trees

78
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:42,640
change color. They are red, orange, and yellow. It's so beautiful. And the weather is not too hot

79
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:48,320
and not too cold. It's perfect for walking. That sounds nice. I think my favorite season

80
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:52,800
is summer. Because you love the hot weather? No, not because of the hot weather. Sometimes

81
00:05:52,800 --> 00:06:00,000
it is too hot. I like summer because the days are long. The sun sets very late. I can go for a walk

82
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:05,920
after dinner. There is still light. I love that. Oh, that is a good point. The long summer days

83
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:12,640
are very nice. You have more time for activities. Exactly. What about spring? What is spring like?

84
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:18,480
Spring is lovely. It comes after winter, the weather gets warmer, the snow melts,

85
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:20,560
the flowers start to grow.

86
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:23,280
You see many beautiful flowers, tulips,

87
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:24,080
daffodils.

88
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,600
It's a happy season.

89
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:28,320
It feels like a new beginning.

90
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:29,120
And winter.

91
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:30,800
Do you like winter?

92
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:33,120
I like winter for a short time.

93
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:34,800
I like it when it snows.

94
00:06:34,880 --> 00:06:37,120
A white Christmas is very beautiful,

95
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,560
but I don't like long cold winters.

96
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:41,160
I get tired of the cold.

97
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:44,360
I don't like wearing heavy clothes every day.

98
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:45,200
I understand.

99
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:46,840
I feel the same.

100
00:06:46,840 --> 00:06:53,360
A little snow is nice, but too much cold is difficult.

101
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:55,280
Driving in snow is also difficult.

102
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:56,880
Yes, it is.

103
00:06:56,880 --> 00:07:00,080
So Jack, what was the weather like last week?

104
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,080
Can you remember?

105
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:03,040
Last week was very strange.

106
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,920
The weather changed every day.

107
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:07,920
It was like four seasons in one week.

108
00:07:07,920 --> 00:07:08,920
It did.

109
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:11,400
On Monday, it was warm and sunny.

110
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:13,200
I remember I didn't wear a jacket.

111
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:17,240
Yes, and on Tuesday it was very, very windy.

112
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:18,360
So windy!

113
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:19,420
I remember.

114
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:21,560
My hat flew off in the wind on Tuesday.

115
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,920
I had to run after it.

116
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:23,920
Oh, that's right.

117
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:25,480
It was very funny.

118
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:29,600
And on Wednesday it was cold and rainy all day.

119
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:32,360
It wasn't just a little rain, it was a lot of rain.

120
00:07:32,360 --> 00:07:34,520
I stayed at home on Wednesday.

121
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:37,000
I drank hot tea and read a book.

122
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,720
It was a good day to be inside.

123
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:41,600
That sounds like a perfect rainy day.

124
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:44,960
And on Thursday, what was the weather like on Thursday?

125
00:07:44,960 --> 00:07:48,520
On Thursday, it was foggy in the morning.

126
00:07:48,520 --> 00:07:54,040
I could only see a few meters in front of me, but in the afternoon, the sun came out and

127
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:55,200
the fog disappeared.

128
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,600
It was nice in the afternoon.

129
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:59,300
And Friday was a beautiful day.

130
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:01,440
It was sunny and warm, just like today.

131
00:08:01,440 --> 00:08:03,600
Yes, Friday was perfect.

132
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:06,280
So the weather is not always the same.

133
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:09,420
It changes every day, sometimes every hour.

134
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:10,760
It changes a lot.

135
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,740
That's why we talk about it so much.

136
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:13,740
It's always different.

137
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:16,040
Let's talk about questions.

138
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:18,680
What questions can we ask about the weather?

139
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:22,520
The easiest question is, what's the weather like?

140
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:23,920
Yes.

141
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,320
What's the weather like?

142
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:28,380
Or what's the weather like today?

143
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:31,200
Or what's the weather like outside?

144
00:08:31,200 --> 00:08:35,160
We can also ask, is it hot outside or is it cold?

145
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:37,080
Or is it raining?

146
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:38,360
Is it sunny?

147
00:08:38,360 --> 00:08:39,640
Is it snowing?

148
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:40,940
And how do we answer?

149
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:45,600
You can say, yes, it is, or no, it isn't.

150
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,600
For example, is it sunny?

151
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:49,440
Yes, it is.

152
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:50,440
Is it raining?

153
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,080
No, it isn't.

154
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:54,280
You can also say, no, it's not.

155
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,760
What about the future?

156
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:58,280
How can we ask about tomorrow's weather?

157
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:01,740
You can ask, what will the weather be like tomorrow?

158
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:04,440
What will the weather be like tomorrow?

159
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:05,940
That's a good question.

160
00:09:05,940 --> 00:09:08,240
It's a little more difficult.

161
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:12,280
You can also ask, is it going to rain tomorrow?

162
00:09:12,280 --> 00:09:13,600
That is very common.

163
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:15,160
And how do we answer?

164
00:09:15,160 --> 00:09:23,200
You can answer with, I think it will be sunny, or the weather forecast says it will rain.

165
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:25,080
The weather forecast?

166
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:29,240
That's the news about the future weather, on TV or on your phone.

167
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:33,760
Yes, many people check the weather forecast every morning.

168
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:35,680
They want to know what to wear.

169
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:37,400
I check it on my phone.

170
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:40,280
I want to know if I need a jacket or an umbrella.

171
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:41,280
It's very useful.

172
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,600
That's very smart.

173
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:44,080
You are learning, Jack.

174
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:45,080
Thank you.

175
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:48,920
So, what do you do on a very hot day?

176
00:09:48,920 --> 00:09:50,040
What activities?

177
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:54,040
On a very hot day, I like to go to the swimming pool.

178
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:56,720
The water is cool and nice.

179
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:58,360
Or I eat ice cream.

180
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:00,000
I stay in the shade.

181
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,840
I don't like to walk in the sun when it is too hot.

182
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:09,360
I like to drink cold water and sit in front of a fan, or I go to an air-conditioned shopping

183
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:10,360
mall.

184
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,360
That's a good idea.

185
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:12,640
The mall is cool.

186
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:16,080
And what do you do on a very cold day?

187
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:20,320
On a very cold day, I wear a thick coat and a warm hat.

188
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:26,360
I drink hot chocolate, I sit near the heater, I watch TV under a warm blanket.

189
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:29,280
That sounds cozy and comfortable.

190
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:30,280
It is.

191
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:33,400
So, Emma, do you think it will rain tomorrow?

192
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:35,360
I don't think so.

193
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:37,760
The sky is very clear today.

194
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:42,360
I think tomorrow will be sunny again, but maybe a little cooler.

195
00:10:42,360 --> 00:10:43,640
I hope you are right.

196
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:45,400
I want to go to the park again.

197
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:47,560
I want to play football with my friends.

198
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:48,720
That sounds fun.

199
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:50,860
I'm sure you will have a good time.

200
00:10:50,860 --> 00:10:55,400
What about extreme weather, like a storm, or thunder and lightning?

201
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:57,460
Oh, that's a bigger topic.

202
00:10:57,460 --> 00:11:02,120
A storm is very strong weather with a lot of wind and rain.

203
00:11:02,120 --> 00:11:06,680
Sometimes you hear thunder, that's the loud sound, and you see lightning.

204
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:08,640
That's the bright light in the sky.

205
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:11,680
I am a little scared of thunderstorms.

206
00:11:11,680 --> 00:11:13,360
The sound is very loud.

207
00:11:13,360 --> 00:11:17,960
It is loud, but it's usually safe inside a building.

208
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:21,560
It's important to stay inside during a storm.

209
00:11:21,560 --> 00:11:23,360
Yes, that's true.

210
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:24,960
What about a breeze?

211
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,400
Is a breeze the same as wind?

212
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:34,120
That's a good question. A breeze is a light wind. It is pleasant. It is not strong. But

213
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:38,660
wind can be strong. A strong wind can be dangerous.

214
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:43,440
So a breeze is nice, but a strong wind is not always nice.

215
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:47,920
Correct. On a hot day, a cool breeze is very nice.

216
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:52,800
Let's talk about the weather in different countries. Is the weather the same in all

217
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:53,800
countries?

218
00:11:53,800 --> 00:12:02,440
it's very different. In countries like Thailand or Brazil, it is often hot and humid. Humid

219
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:08,120
means there is a lot of water in the air. And in countries like Canada or Norway, it

220
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:15,520
is often very cold and snowy in winter. Yes. And in some countries like England, it

221
00:12:15,520 --> 00:12:20,600
is often cloudy and rainy. They talk about the weather all the time there. I think

222
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:26,680
I would need an umbrella every day in England probably so when you travel you

223
00:12:26,680 --> 00:12:31,200
need to check the weather for that country that is very important you need

224
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:37,560
to pack the right clothes exactly if you go to a hot country you pack t-shirts

225
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:44,200
and shorts if you go to a cold country you pack a warm coat and gloves so the

226
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:49,560
weather is important for travel for clothes for activities for everything it

227
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:54,000
It is. That's why it's such a useful topic to talk about.

228
00:12:54,000 --> 00:13:01,200
Let's practice a little dialogue. Imagine I'm your neighbor. I see you outside. I say,

229
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:04,340
Good morning, Emma. Lovely day, isn't it?

230
00:13:04,340 --> 00:13:09,960
And I say, Yes, it's a beautiful day. So sunny and warm.

231
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:14,600
Then I say, I hope it stays like this for the weekend. I want to have a picnic.

232
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:17,160
And I say, that sounds nice.

233
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:18,880
I think the weather will be good.

234
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:20,280
The forecast is good.

235
00:13:20,280 --> 00:13:21,400
Perfect.

236
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:23,440
That was a very natural conversation.

237
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:24,280
It was.

238
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:25,520
You see, it's easy.

239
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:28,280
What about a different situation?

240
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:30,840
It's a rainy Monday morning.

241
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,800
I see you at the bus stop.

242
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:35,920
I say, oh, what a rainy day.

243
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:39,720
And I say, I know, I don't like Monday mornings

244
00:13:39,720 --> 00:13:41,000
and the rain doesn't help.

245
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:44,160
Yes, it's a difficult start to the week.

246
00:13:44,160 --> 00:13:45,360
Do you have an umbrella?

247
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:48,440
And I say, yes, I have one today.

248
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:49,720
I remembered.

249
00:13:49,720 --> 00:13:50,800
Very good.

250
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:52,220
You were learning from me, Emma.

251
00:13:52,220 --> 00:13:53,400
I am.

252
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,760
So we can talk about the weather

253
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:57,800
in many different situations.

254
00:13:57,800 --> 00:13:59,560
It's a very flexible topic.

255
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:01,400
And it helps us start a conversation.

256
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:03,920
It helps us connect with people.

257
00:14:03,920 --> 00:14:06,380
That's a beautiful way to say it, Jack.

258
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,440
It helps us connect with people.

259
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:10,560
So everyone practice this.

260
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:12,800
Talk about the weather with someone today.

261
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:14,000
It's good practice.

262
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,760
Yes, please try it, you can do it.

263
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:21,760
Emma, we talked about so many weather words.

264
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:23,880
My brain is full.

265
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:26,280
It is a lot of information.

266
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:30,240
Maybe we should slow down and review some of the keywords.

267
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,880
Let's do a small vocabulary review.

268
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,320
That's a great idea.

269
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:36,120
It will help us remember.

270
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:38,460
What words should we talk about first?

271
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:41,240
Let's start with the word temperature.

272
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:43,160
We use this word a lot.

273
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:44,960
Temperature, yes.

274
00:14:44,960 --> 00:14:48,600
Temperature tells us how hot or cold it is.

275
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:49,520
That's right.

276
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:50,840
It's a measurement.

277
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:53,360
We measure temperature in degrees.

278
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:58,040
For example, today it is 22 degrees Celsius.

279
00:14:58,040 --> 00:14:59,720
That's a warm temperature.

280
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:05,320
And if it is 35 degrees Celsius, that is a very hot temperature.

281
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:09,640
If it is 5 degrees Celsius, that is a cold temperature.

282
00:15:09,640 --> 00:15:10,640
Perfect!

283
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:14,440
So, you can ask, what is the temperature today?

284
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:17,720
And you can answer, it is 22 degrees.

285
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:18,720
Exactly.

286
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:22,760
The next word is very useful, forecast.

287
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:24,480
The weather forecast.

288
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:26,000
I love this word.

289
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,960
I check the forecast every day.

290
00:15:28,960 --> 00:15:36,880
is a forecast. A forecast is a prediction. It tells us the future weather. So, the

291
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:43,740
weather forecast tells us if it will be sunny or rainy tomorrow. Yes, for example,

292
00:15:43,740 --> 00:15:49,720
you can say the weather forecast is good for Saturday. We can have our picnic. Or

293
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:56,380
the forecast says it will be cold next week. Good. Now, let's talk about different

294
00:15:56,380 --> 00:15:59,820
types of rain. We have the word drizzle.

295
00:16:00,140 --> 00:16:05,220
Drizzle? What does drizzle mean? Is it the same as rain?

296
00:16:05,660 --> 00:16:10,220
It is a type of rain, but it is very light rain.

297
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:15,060
Drizzle is not heavy. The water drops are very small.

298
00:16:15,460 --> 00:16:18,460
You don't always need an umbrella for a drizzle.

299
00:16:18,980 --> 00:16:22,820
Oh, I understand. So if it is drizzling,

300
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:26,820
It is raining but only a little bit, it's not a problem.

301
00:16:26,820 --> 00:16:31,320
Yes, you can say, it's not raining hard, it's just drizzling.

302
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:34,320
I like that word. It sounds gentle.

303
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:36,820
What is the opposite of drizzle?

304
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:39,820
The opposite is a downpour.

305
00:16:39,820 --> 00:16:42,820
A downpour is very, very heavy rain.

306
00:16:42,820 --> 00:16:45,820
A lot of rain falls in a short time.

307
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:50,320
Oh, in a downpour, you definitely need an umbrella.

308
00:16:50,320 --> 00:16:57,640
you probably need to wait inside for a few minutes. Exactly. For example, we were

309
00:16:57,640 --> 00:17:04,960
walking in the park when suddenly there was a downpour. We got very wet! Okay, so

310
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:10,880
we have drizzle for light rain and downpour for heavy rain. Now let's talk

311
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:18,440
about wind. We already know windy, but there's another word, breeze. A breeze.

312
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:27,520
Is a breeze strong? No, a breeze is a light, gentle wind. It is pleasant and nice. On a hot day,

313
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:35,560
a cool breeze feels wonderful. So, if the wind is strong and moves the trees a lot, we say it's

314
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:43,040
windy, but if the wind is soft and gentle, we can say it's a breezy day or there is a nice breeze.

315
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:50,360
Yes, that's a very good way to explain it. You can say, I love sitting here. There's a lovely breeze.

316
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:57,720
Okay, next word. What about humid? You said this word before.

317
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:06,800
Ah, humid. This is an important word. Humid means the air has a lot of water in it. The air feels

318
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:09,000
wet and heavy.

319
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:13,200
So it's not raining, but the air feels wet?

320
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:20,720
Yes. On a humid day, you might sweat more. Your skin feels sticky. It often feels hotter

321
00:18:20,720 --> 00:18:23,520
than it really is because of the humidity.

322
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:29,440
I don't like humid days. I prefer dry air. Dry air feels more comfortable.

323
00:18:29,440 --> 00:18:35,960
Many people agree with you. So you can say, today is so hot and humid, or the humidity

324
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:38,240
is very high today.

325
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:40,600
I will remember that.

326
00:18:40,600 --> 00:18:42,860
Let's talk about cold weather.

327
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:45,080
We have the word chilly.

328
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:47,180
Yes, chilly.

329
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:49,120
What does chilly mean?

330
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:51,320
Is it the same as cold?

331
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:54,920
I think chilly is a little cold.

332
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:58,960
It is not very cold, but it is not warm.

333
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:02,680
You feel a little cold, so you might want a light jacket.

334
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:04,160
That's exactly right.

335
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:11,040
is between cool and cold. It's a common word. You can say, the morning is quite chilly,

336
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:16,360
but the afternoon will be warmer. Or, there's a chilly wind today.

337
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:23,720
Perfect. Now, one more important word. Clear. Clear. Like clear water?

338
00:19:23,720 --> 00:19:31,520
Similar idea. For weather, a clear sky means there are no clouds. The sky is blue and empty.

339
00:19:31,520 --> 00:19:33,940
You can see the sun very well.

340
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:37,180
So a clear night is good for looking at the stars.

341
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:40,780
Yes, and a clear day is good for taking photos.

342
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:44,380
The opposite of clear is cloudy or overcast.

343
00:19:44,380 --> 00:19:45,380
Overcast?

344
00:19:45,380 --> 00:19:48,140
That's a new word.

345
00:19:48,140 --> 00:19:52,580
Overcast means the sky is completely covered with clouds.

346
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:54,660
You cannot see the sun.

347
00:19:54,660 --> 00:19:56,540
It is often gray.

348
00:19:56,540 --> 00:19:57,900
It is more than cloudy.

349
00:19:57,900 --> 00:19:59,980
It is fully covered.

350
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:07,440
So cloudy can mean some clouds, but overcast means 100% clouds.

351
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:08,440
Yes.

352
00:20:08,440 --> 00:20:13,800
For example, the sky was overcast all day, but it didn't rain.

353
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:15,640
This is very useful.

354
00:20:15,640 --> 00:20:17,620
So let's list our words again.

355
00:20:17,620 --> 00:20:27,480
We have temperature, forecast, drizzle, downpour, breeze, humid, chilly, and clear.

356
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:28,480
And overcast!

357
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:29,960
That's nine words!

358
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:31,720
You learned a lot today, Jack.

359
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:34,360
I think our viewers learned a lot too.

360
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:37,320
Let's try to use them all in a small story.

361
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:39,600
Okay, you start.

362
00:20:39,600 --> 00:20:40,600
Okay.

363
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:43,760
Yesterday, I checked the weather forecast.

364
00:20:43,760 --> 00:20:48,400
The temperature was 10 degrees, so I knew it would be chilly.

365
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:52,460
In the morning, the sky was clear and beautiful.

366
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:53,660
Very good.

367
00:20:53,660 --> 00:20:57,600
But in the afternoon, the sky became overcast.

368
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:59,680
Then it started to drizzle.

369
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:03,340
I didn't have an umbrella, but it was only a drizzle.

370
00:21:03,340 --> 00:21:07,700
Then the drizzle stopped and a nice cool breeze started.

371
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:09,660
It was perfect.

372
00:21:09,660 --> 00:21:16,060
But my friend in another city said they had a downpour and their weather is always very

373
00:21:16,060 --> 00:21:17,260
humid.

374
00:21:17,260 --> 00:21:18,360
We did it.

375
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:19,860
We used all the words.

376
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:21,860
That was excellent practice.

377
00:21:21,860 --> 00:21:22,860
It was.

378
00:21:22,860 --> 00:21:25,700
Everyone, these words are very common.

379
00:21:25,700 --> 00:21:29,060
Try to use one or two of them this week.

380
00:21:29,060 --> 00:21:32,500
Well, Jack, we talked for a very long time today.

381
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,440
My voice is a little tired.

382
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:37,900
My voice is tired, too, but it was a good conversation.

383
00:21:37,900 --> 00:21:40,960
I think we covered so many things about the weather.

384
00:21:40,960 --> 00:21:42,900
We really did.

385
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:46,660
Let's take a moment to summarize what we practiced today.

386
00:21:46,660 --> 00:21:48,060
It's good to review.

387
00:21:48,060 --> 00:21:49,820
Okay, let's do it.

388
00:21:49,820 --> 00:21:53,940
First, we learned how to describe the weather in simple words.

389
00:21:53,940 --> 00:22:00,700
We used sunny, rainy, windy, snowy, cloudy, and foggy.

390
00:22:00,700 --> 00:22:02,000
That's right.

391
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,260
Those are the basic adjectives.

392
00:22:04,260 --> 00:22:09,580
We can say, it is sunny, or it is a sunny day.

393
00:22:09,580 --> 00:22:11,540
And then we talked about temperature.

394
00:22:11,540 --> 00:22:16,100
We learned hot, warm, cool, and cold.

395
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:17,300
Yes.

396
00:22:17,300 --> 00:22:25,000
So you can say, it is a warm sunny day, or it is a cold, rainy night.

397
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:27,160
We also learned how to ask questions.

398
00:22:27,160 --> 00:22:31,720
The most important question is, what's the weather like?

399
00:22:31,720 --> 00:22:37,760
And what's the weather like today, and what will the weather be like tomorrow?

400
00:22:37,760 --> 00:22:43,160
And the answer is, it's sunny, or I think it will be cold.

401
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:46,580
Then we had a big vocabulary review.

402
00:22:46,580 --> 00:22:49,200
We learned some very useful new words.

403
00:22:49,200 --> 00:22:51,160
Can you remember some of them, Jack?

404
00:22:51,160 --> 00:22:52,520
I'll try.

405
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:56,920
We had temperature, that's how hot or cold it is.

406
00:22:56,920 --> 00:22:57,920
Good.

407
00:22:57,920 --> 00:23:02,080
We had forecast, that's the prediction for the future weather.

408
00:23:02,080 --> 00:23:05,020
Yes, always check the forecast.

409
00:23:05,020 --> 00:23:12,220
We had drizzle, for very light rain, and downpour, for very heavy rain.

410
00:23:12,220 --> 00:23:14,980
Very good, you remembered the opposites.

411
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:22,540
We had breeze for a nice gentle wind and humid for when the air feels wet and sticky.

412
00:23:22,540 --> 00:23:23,580
Perfect.

413
00:23:23,580 --> 00:23:31,100
We had chilly for weather that is a little cold and clear for a sky with no clouds.

414
00:23:31,100 --> 00:23:32,780
And one more?

415
00:23:32,780 --> 00:23:36,300
What about a completely gray sky?

416
00:23:36,300 --> 00:23:38,340
Oh, overcast.

417
00:23:38,340 --> 00:23:42,540
That's when the sky is 100% covered with clouds.

418
00:23:42,540 --> 00:23:43,540
Excellent memory, Jack.

419
00:23:43,540 --> 00:23:44,540
I'm impressed.

420
00:23:44,540 --> 00:23:51,900
Thank you. I was paying attention. So we learned a lot of words and how to use them in conversations.

421
00:23:51,900 --> 00:23:57,500
We also talked about our favorite seasons and what we do in different types of weather.

422
00:23:57,500 --> 00:24:03,580
Yes, like drinking hot chocolate on a cold day or going to the pool on a hot day.

423
00:24:03,580 --> 00:24:09,980
And we even practiced a few short dialogues like neighbors talking about the weather.

424
00:24:09,980 --> 00:24:16,220
That was fun. I think the most important thing is that talking about the weather is easy

425
00:24:16,220 --> 00:24:23,100
and friendly. It's a way to be social. It is. It's a way to start a conversation with anyone.

426
00:24:23,900 --> 00:24:29,820
So we hope you feel more confident now. Yes, please don't be shy. Try to use these words.

427
00:24:30,620 --> 00:24:36,860
And now it's time for our favorite part of the video. The question of the day.

428
00:24:36,860 --> 00:24:43,860
Today's question is all about you and your opinions.

429
00:24:43,860 --> 00:24:49,420
The question is, what is your favorite type of weather and why?

430
00:24:49,420 --> 00:24:51,660
So what do you like?

431
00:24:51,660 --> 00:24:54,260
Do you like sunny weather like Jack?

432
00:24:54,260 --> 00:24:56,900
Or do you like rainy weather like Emma?

433
00:24:56,900 --> 00:25:00,020
Or maybe you like snowy weather.

434
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:07,600
Tell us exactly what your favorite weather is, and most importantly, tell us why.

435
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:09,000
Why do you like it?

436
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:15,040
For example, you can write, my favorite weather is sunny and warm.

437
00:25:15,040 --> 00:25:16,320
Why?

438
00:25:16,320 --> 00:25:19,360
Because I can go to the beach and swim in the sea.

439
00:25:19,360 --> 00:25:24,720
Or, my favorite weather is cold and snowy.

440
00:25:24,720 --> 00:25:26,160
Why?

441
00:25:26,160 --> 00:25:29,480
Because I can make a snowman with my family.

442
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:36,080
or my favorite weather is rainy. Why? Because I love the sound of rain and I can read my

443
00:25:36,080 --> 00:25:37,560
book inside.

444
00:25:37,560 --> 00:25:43,640
There are no wrong answers. We are all different and we like different things.

445
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:49,920
Please tell us your answer in the comments below this video. We read every single comment.

446
00:25:49,920 --> 00:25:56,120
We really do. We love to read your comments and see you practicing English. It makes

447
00:25:56,120 --> 00:25:58,080
us very happy.

448
00:25:58,080 --> 00:26:02,800
And if you have a friend who is also learning English, please share this video with them.

449
00:26:02,800 --> 00:26:04,320
You can practice together.

450
00:26:04,320 --> 00:26:06,560
That's a wonderful idea.

451
00:26:06,560 --> 00:26:09,320
Learning with a friend is more fun.

452
00:26:09,320 --> 00:26:15,260
Also, if you enjoyed this lesson, please let us know by liking this video.

